hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2959","###\n Narrated to us by Al-Abbas ibn al-Abbas and Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: Narrated to us by Sufyan, from Al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, who said: \I witnessed the Eid prayer with Umar ibn al-Khattab (RA). He said: 'Indeed"","" the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade fasting on these two days. As for the Day of Fitr"","" it is the day of breaking your fast from your fasting. And as"""""
